<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Zedillo to sign six accords in China.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Zedillo to sign six accords in China.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican President Ernesto Zedillo is scheduled to sign six bilateral agreements during his forthcoming state visit to China, a government spokesman said Tuesday.</p>
<p>The agreements will cover areas such as the economy, diplomacy, the war on drugs and farm production, Deputy Minister for Bilateral Affairs Juan Rebolledo said.</p>
<p>Zedillo will be in the People's Republic of China from Thursday to Sunday.</p>
<p>Two-way trade between Mexico and China totalled $558 million in 1995.</p>
<p>--Debora Montesinos, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7915</p>
</text>
